%% KDS overview only. Focused diagrams below prove ingestion, Redis projection, realtime hint/refetch, and ticket mutation.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Kafka as Kafka<br/>order.confirmed
  participant Kitchen as Kitchen<br/>KDS service
  participant Redis as Redis<br/>KDS projection
  participant BFF as BFF<br/>realtime edge
  participant UI as KDS client
  actor Chef as Chef / Barista
  participant Order as Order<br/>item lifecycle

  Kafka->>Kitchen: Deliver order.confirmed
  Kitchen->>Kitchen: Validate contract and split by station
  Kitchen->>Redis: Create station tickets<br/>queue + revision + SLA
  Kitchen->>BFF: Publish kds.queue_changed hint
  BFF-->>UI: WebSocket hint
  UI->>BFF: Refetch queue snapshot
  BFF->>Kitchen: TCP get station queue
  Kitchen->>Redis: Read authoritative projection
  Kitchen-->>BFF: Queue snapshot
  BFF-->>UI: Latest KDS state

  Chef->>UI: Start / mark ready ticket
  UI->>BFF: Protected KDS command
  BFF->>Kitchen: TCP ticket mutation
  Kitchen->>Redis: Update ticket status and revision
  opt Ticket marked READY
    BFF->>Order: Sync ready order items
    Order-->>BFF: Item readiness result
  end
  Kitchen->>BFF: Publish queue changed hint
  BFF-->>UI: WebSocket hint, client refetches

  Note over UI,BFF: WebSocket is only a hint. The client refetches the queue snapshot from the server.
